NXR-221|Monitor legal transition table|Target executive|The target executive shall enforce the documented command-state transition table without implicit starts.|The proposed states need executable rejection tests as well as happy-path scenarios.|CONFIGURE, ARM, START, STOP and REARM issued in every state either follow the table or fail unchanged.|Exhaustively exercise the finite state-command matrix including duplicate commands.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Fixed state enum and one active run; bounded command processing.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|The proposed states need executable rejection tests as well as happy-path scenarios.
NXR-222|All-worker start barrier|Target executive|RUNNING shall be reported only after every selected worker acknowledges the same run generation.|Dispatching START does not prove that all required workers became active.|Delay or omit one worker acknowledgement; the monitor remains starting or fails its deadline without claiming full activity.|Gate workers individually and compare acknowledgements with externally observed activity.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|One acknowledgement bit per configured worker and finite start deadline.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|Dispatching START does not prove that all required workers became active.
NXR-223|Stop ownership reconciliation|Target executive|COMPLETED shall require all selected workers quiescent and all test-owned resources reconciled.|Worker inactivity is insufficient when hardware or descriptors still own buffers.|A pending DMA transfer or unreturned queue descriptor prevents COMPLETED even if worker loops have ended.|Hold each resource type in turn and verify stop classification and residual inventory.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Finite reconciliation pass over declared test resources.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|Worker inactivity is insufficient when hardware or descriptors still own buffers.
NXR-224|Rearm control-queue preservation|Target executive|REARM shall reset only settled test resources and preserve permanent monitor control channels.|Permanent control waiters are legitimate idle state and must not be drained as leaked test resources.|An idle control waiter survives REARM and accepts the next command; stale job descriptors are rejected.|Repeat configure-run-stop-rearm cycles with queued old-generation work and idle control waiters.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|No blanket queue reset; fixed run-generation metadata.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|Permanent control waiters are legitimate idle state and must not be drained as leaked test resources.
NXR-225|Fault state quiescence distinction|Target executive|FAULTED shall report quiescence independently and forbid reuse when ownership remains uncertain.|A fault label is not proof that external activity has stopped.|Inject a worker fault during active DMA; fault evidence is retained while reuse remains blocked.|Model fault and stop transitions and inspect hardware ownership until reset.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Separate fault and quiescence fields; one retained first-fault slot.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|A fault label is not proof that external activity has stopped.
NXR-226|Monitor noninterference budget|Target executive|The monitor shall publish its priority, sampling cost and transport budget so test results account for observer load.|The test executive can perturb the scheduler behavior it is measuring.|Compare workload progress with telemetry disabled and enabled; overhead stays within the predeclared envelope.|Measure target cycles and external GPIO timing under summary and trace modes.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Default summary rate one per second; fixed service budget per dispatch.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|The test executive can perturb the scheduler behavior it is measuring.
NXR-227|Command descriptor ownership|Target executive|Monitor queues shall carry bounded frame descriptors rather than copying full 512-byte packets under the kernel queue lock.|The fixed packet size exceeds the existing queue copy limit and needs separate frame storage.|Largest command enqueue respects the 128-byte copy limit; descriptor ownership is conserved on reject and cancel.|Fill every pool slot and inject parse failures, duplicate responses and cancellation.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Static frame pool and descriptor queue; proposed protocol storage ceiling 6784 bytes excluding stacks and descriptors.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|The fixed packet size exceeds the existing queue copy limit and needs separate frame storage.
NXR-228|Terminal evidence acknowledgement|Target executive|The monitor shall retain final result and fault records until the host acknowledges the matching logical identity.|A transport write success does not establish durable host receipt.|Drop result frames and reconnect; identical logical evidence remains fetchable and is not replaced by a new run.|Exercise lost acknowledgement, duplicate fetch and stale acknowledgement cases.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|One retained terminal result and first fault; finite fetch payloads.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|A transport write success does not establish durable host receipt.
NXR-229|Monitor parameter validation|Target executive|CONFIGURE shall validate worker selection, job bounds, durations and resource needs before changing the active configuration.|Malformed test parameters can invalidate the resource guarantees of an otherwise bounded workload.|Overflowing durations, zero illegal counts and excessive frame demand fail without partial resource acquisition.|Test each parameter boundary and a compound invalid configuration against state snapshots.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|Checked arithmetic and declared fixed capacities; no allocation on configure.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|Malformed test parameters can invalidate the resource guarantees of an otherwise bounded workload.
NXR-230|Sacrificial worker reboot policy|Target executive|A test that permanently exits a boot-created worker shall declare the run non-rearmable without the required reset.|Current exit semantics reserve storage and do not permit recreating finished workers.|After exit the monitor reports reboot required and rejects another run needing that worker.|Run exit-focused fixtures and then attempt rearm and start with the same worker inventory.|NXR-039,NXR-048|Opt-in qualification profile; boot-static storage; single CPU unless explicitly qualified otherwise.|No runtime thread resurrection in the default kernel profile.|src/kernel.cpp,docs/hil-verification-plan.rst,include/rtos_queue.hpp|Current exit semantics reserve storage and do not permit recreating finished workers.
